    {
      "benchmark": "extrema",
      "title": "Scientific output storage does not determine counted FLOPs",
      "observation": "The extrema contract visits Int32/Int64/Float32/Float64 inputs but produces Boolean comparison masks; ordinary add/multiply/FMA work must come from actual counters, not its input type. Conversely, DXT compression emits packed integer words after floating endpoint search and integer packing. Storage/output type is separate from executed precision and scientific semantics.",
